      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Mix lemon juice, garlic, chilli, oil and salt. Pour over chicken and marinate for at least 2 hours in the fridge. Reserve the marinade."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Heat a griddle pan over high heat. Grill chicken for 4 minutes per side until charred in places. Set aside."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Heat 3 tablespoons oil in a large saucepan. Add all the sliced onion and cook over medium heat for 35 to 40 minutes, stirring every 5 minutes, until deep golden and very soft."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Add the reserved marinade, bay leaves and black pepper. Stir and cook for 3 minutes."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Nestle the grilled chicken into the onions. Cover and cook on medium-low for 20 minutes until chicken is cooked through and the sauce has reduced."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Cook rice separately. Serve the chicken and sauce over rice."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "symptom": "Sauce too sharp",
              "cause": "Not enough caramelisation on the onions",
              "fix": "The sweetness of the caramelised onions balances the lemon. Cook onions until they are genuinely golden, not just softened."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "symptom": "Onions catching and burning",
              "cause": "Heat too high or pan too dry",
              "fix": "Add a splash of water and stir. Reduce heat to medium-low and continue slowly."
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Where this dish lives"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Yassa originated among the Diola people of the Casamance region in southern Senegal. It is now one of the most widely cooked dishes in the country and appears in West African restaurants worldwide. Fish yassa (yassa poisson) is an equally popular variation using the same marinade. The dish has crossed into Gambia and Guinea-Bissau where versions vary in chilli heat and onion depth."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
